Negative control for the manager's refused-reply outcome (AC17).

Puts the page back to ignoring `reply()`'s return value: the composer is cleared
and no notice is raised whatever the call resolved with. A `409
ticket_has_more_recent_reply` resolves to `undefined` rather than throwing, so
nothing errors, nothing is posted, and the client's words are gone — the page
reports a send it never made. The SUCCESS path is untouched and stays green,
which is the point: only a spec that drives the REFUSAL goes red.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: `client-ticket-reply-stale.spec.ts` — "a reply REFUSED with 409
ticket_has_more_recent_reply keeps the draft and says it was not sent", and the
no-re-post case beside it.

